  palliative care (PC) alone. Short-term change in quality of life (QOL) was assessed in a subgroup of patients. Data   
  from the two trials were combined to allow multivariate and stratified survival analyses. RESULTS Seven hundred       
  ninety-seven eligible patients were randomized, 446 in MIC1 and 351 in MIC2. MIC CT improved survival in both trials  
